regress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth\panel_20260912_095238_ppcpass2\codex.txt:2453:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lunaabsentcpu\opus_p1.md:14:Option (a) is measured correct and complete for the witness. But the detector plan as written **fails vacuity-floor clause (d)**: I built the clause-(d) null-repair mutant (`d->ncpus = 1;` hardcoded) and it scored **20/20 — a total escape — on the 1-cpu detector**. It is killed by exactly one thing: the `-n 2` accept row observing cpu 1 asserting. **The accept row is mandatory, not optional.** A second mutant (`ncpus` never assigned) escapes every survival and readback row and is killed only by a free-running delivery row on the *default* 1-cpu config.
