regress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth\panel_20260912_095238_ppcpass2\codex.txt:2527:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\codex_escapes_20260910.txt:21:  Its observable defect is the extra bits in stored readback. The acceptance guard remains, while filtering of the `v` its body stores is partly nulled: clause (d)’s repair-mask case.
regress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth\panel_20260912_095238_ppcpass2\codex.txt:2528:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\codex_escapes_20260910.txt:49:These classifications follow the “guard kept, repair nulled” rule and this instrument’s explicit per-arm store-mask contract. They do not require treating every edited statement as a predicate. None touches an unchanged `W_T_BASE` arm. See the [repair implementation](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_lca.c:377), [clause (d)](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/CLAUDE.md:1287), and [frozen contract](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/lcabadval/killtable_20260910/t4/lca_badval_probe.REPAIRED67.asrun.py:338).
