regress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth\panel_20260912_095238_ppcpass2\codex.txt:2598:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\pass2_79cd12e\seats\grok.txt:1:I'll treat this as a real pass-2, not a ratification: first I'll pull HEAD/checkpoint/queue truth, then read the shipped product code and detectors against the brief's premises.Git from the shell was blocked, so I’m reading the shipped sources, detectors, and CHANGELOG directly and will re-derive the premises from those.The comments’ arithmetic checks out; next I’ll verify ncpus mutation, raise sites, and whether a one-token bound or `implemented` edit actually escapes the shipped detectors.**VERDICT: GO-WITH-CHANGES.** Both product fixes are in the right place. `#503`'s `ncpus` snapshot is stable. `#502`'s C diff delivers all seven classes at both sites — it is not a `#499` one-cell repair. The `#502` detector, asked of the shipped composite, has one clause-(d) mutant I predict sweeps **59/59**: `implemented = true` → `implemented = (cpu->machine->ncpus < 2)` on the seven arms. I could not build it (read-only seat; gates forbidden). If that score is real it is **L2 of the detector**, not of `cpu_m88k.c`. `#503`'s single-token / operand-swap set is closed on the counts the probe actually boots.
