regress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth\panel_20260912_095238_ppcpass2\codex.txt:2721:_scratchpad\panel_20260910_202650\ollama_glm.txt:49:Strongest form: (a) the packet never says who enumerated the nine (d) mutants — if the measuring seat enumerated M15/M20–27 itself, measured its own prescribed form failing against its own mutants, then expanded its own instrument to kill them, the closure is self-referential and the "five measured sweeps" are evidence only about a class the seat invented; (b) a reviewed prescription was overridden 3× by 152 unreviewed lines receiving their first panel now; (c) the sharpest version — 40 of 59 rows now lean on the least-structurally-guaranteed oracle in the instrument, the uninitialised stack the vacuity caution warned about; (d) the 59-row denominator permanently breaks comparability with the 14/19-row baselines. Why it loses: the driving escapes, M13 and M14, pre-date the seat and were measured against two shipped instruments (READ) — a floor whose declined set sits off-domain is a floor over the rows you happen to have, not over the store's reachable behavior. (c) argues for a *different* instrument (two-paint), not a smaller one; (a) belongs on the record — name the enumerator; (d) is bookkeeping. And per P1, the creep was twelve cells, not ten — the author should re-run his own arithmetic before defending the number. Expansion justified; adopt the two-paint fix and log the enumerator.
