5228:# `#527` (ppcrlwimiwidth, ppcrldimimask): two PowerPC rotate-and-insert instructions computed wrong results - `rlwimi` rotated a 32-bit word at 64-bit width and never wrote a wrapping mask's high word; `rldimi`'s rotate loop consumed its own shift count, so every insert mask was built from `sh == -1`
5229:
5230:Both are sibling handlers in `src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c` and share one commit and one joint kill table,
5231:because one build exercises both and each probe is the other's cross-check.  The architecture is Book I
5232:v2.01 (`_scratchpad/ppc_uisa_book1_v201.txt`): rlwimi `r <- ROTL32((RS)32:63, SH); m <- MASK(MB+32,
5233:ME+32); RA <- (r & m) | ((RA) & ~m)` with MASK wrapping when x > y (`:578`), and ROTL32 duplicating the
5234:word into both halves; rldimi `r <- ROTL64((RS), sh); m <- MASK(mb, 63-sh)`.
5235:
5236:**rlwimi - two defects in one handler.**  (1) `MODE_uint_t tmp = reg(rs)` held all 64 bits, so
5237:`(tmp << sh) | (tmp >> (32 - sh))` pulled high-word bits DOWN into the rotated low word.  (2) A
5238:wrapping mask (MB > ME) covers the WHOLE high word, which must receive the rotated word; the handler
5239:only walked the low word.  **FIX:** narrow on read, `uint32_t tmp = (uint32_t)reg(rs)`, and BEFORE the
5240:insertion loop `if (mb > me) ra = (ra & 0xffffffffULL) | ((uint64_t)tmp << 32);` - before, because the
5241:loop walks `mb` to `me` and a guard placed after it would never fire (`R_POST_LOOP` measures exactly
5242:that).  A 19-line comment records why a 32-bit `MODE_uint_t` build keeps only the low word, and that this
5243:is NOT a claim that 32-bit MODE removes half the register (Book I 1.2).
5244:
5245:**rldimi - two defects in one handler.**  (1) `while (sh-- != 0)` rotated correctly and left `sh == -1`,
5246:so the mask end `63 - sh` was 64 for every encoding.  (2) The mask loop `m ++` never wrapped past bit 63.
5247:**FIX:** rotate a copy (`int m, n = sh;  while (n-- != 0)`) and make the loop circular
5248:(`m = (m + 1) & 63; } while (m != ((64 - sh) & 63))`).
5249:
5250:**WITNESSES, rung 3, unmodified in-tree `-E bareppc -M 64` (PPC970).**  rlwimi: committed **14/28**, fix
5251:**28/28** (`artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth/witness_{committed,fix}.out`, agy's witness).  rldimi: committed
5252:**17/27**, fix **27/27** (`artifacts/ppcrldimimask/witness_*.out`, the Opus seat's).  No Book I error in
5253:either fix: codex checked all 32,768 rlwimi and 4,096 rldimi immediate combinations against a model of
5254:the RTL; grok and kimi re-derived both from Book I independently.
