19:**Q5 - readiness.** **xscaleinten: YES** once `gate_arm.sh` runs green at pin 30 (wired, verified), with the CHANGELOG grading RD0_ALLONES as L1/(e) under the Q1 rule, F2's scope stated per codex, and F7/F11's kill channels named (`host-death`, `liveness`). **PPC: YES after four owed items, none a row:** (i) restore `_scratchpad/gate_ppc.ppcround.sh` into `gate_ppc.sh` and verify its pins equal the shipped probes' row counts (28, 29) at restore time - a green existing gate proves nothing about this delivery; (ii) rewrite the F15 record as above; (iii) carry the F11 caveat and `CENSUS_SHRINK`; (iv) **scope `regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py`** - it is modified in the working tree (78 lines, a `mask_range` oracle correction citing `ppcwitnessmaskoracle`) and must either enter this commit with its own record line or be excluded by name, never ride in unlabelled; the same goes for the `tools/*` and `fable_queue.md` modifications. F14 is DISCHARGED (rlwimi header clause (4) is in the tree; codex/grok/kimi read a pre-edit copy). If the SH=63 row or the Rc destination check is taken, add the table-4 legs and pin bump to the list; if not, file both with their specs. Product code: unchanged, correctly.

