    #527 (ppcrlwimiwidth, ppcrldimimask): rlwimi rotated a 32-bit word at 64-bit width and never wrote a wrapping mask's high word; rldimi's rotate loop consumed its shift count
    
    Two sibling handlers in src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c, against Book I v2.01.
    
    rlwimi: `MODE_uint_t tmp = reg(rs)` held all 64 bits, so the 32-bit rotate pulled
    high-word bits into the low word; and a wrapping mask (MB > ME) covers the whole
    high word, which must receive the rotated word, while the handler walked only the
    low word.  Fix: `uint32_t tmp = (uint32_t)reg(rs)`, and BEFORE the insertion loop
    `if (mb > me) ra = (ra & 0xffffffffULL) | ((uint64_t)tmp << 32);`.
    
    rldimi: `while (sh-- != 0)` left sh == -1, so the mask end was 64 for every
    encoding, and the mask loop never wrapped past bit 63.  Fix: rotate a copy
    (`n = sh`) and make the loop circular (`m = (m + 1) & 63` until
    `(64 - sh) & 63`).
    
    WITNESSES, rung 3, unmodified -E bareppc -M 64: rlwimi committed 14/28, fix
    28/28; rldimi committed 17/27, fix 27/27.  codex checked every rlwimi and rldimi
    immediate combination against Book I's RTL: no error in either fix.
    
    DETECTORS: regress/ppc_rlwimi_probe.py (28 rows) and ppc_rldimi_probe.py (29),
    wired into gate_ppc.sh BEFORE its NetBSD prerequisite, parse-before-score, pins
    28 and 29.  Joint kill table 3 (one build per leg, both probes, the other
    probe as cross-check): 17 legs, 15 on prediction, zero escapes; the two misses
    (D_NO_MERGE arithmetic; D_NOCIRC under undefined shifts) are recorded.
    
    PASS 2 found two rldimi gaps, both closed by an L1 row that is each mutant's
    sole killer: codex's rotate skip confined to full-width masks (`full rot`), and
    glm's rA == rS gap -- whose literal mutant turned out, on simulation, not to be
    an aliasing mutant at all; the built form is its own "equivalently".  Fable
    5.1, fired last and verified by its own model name, ruled codex's three later
    gaps clause (e) and closed the repair chain; it also found my F15 record wrong:
    narrowing tmp made the existing `sh ?` guard load-bearing (tmp >> 32 is
    undefined at SH = 0).  Filed with specs, not built: an SH=63 full-mask row,
    a wrap-only alias re-read, an Rc=1-only skip, CENSUS_SHRINK, R_NOGUARD.
    
    Gate 13 PASS, 110 checks, every rlwimi/rldimi row ok, from a frozen copy
    (artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth/gate_ppc_20260912.log).  Gate-section negative controls
    11/11 as specified (gate_negctl_20260912.sh/.out).  Two-part clearance run
    before the gate: cpu_ppc_instr.c p1=CLEAN p2=FRESH in build/, build-asan/ and
    /tmp/gxsec-build; est/ p1=CLEAN, p2 N/A.
    
    Also: SCORE_CLAIMS_MANIFEST 25 -> 28, the third being #526's xscale pin, which
    #526 shipped quoted and invisible to the score-claims check -- unquoted here;
    #526's pass-2 receipt and ledger commits field.  NOT in this commit, by name:
    regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py (an earlier session's unreviewed oracle re-pin) and
    the tools/ carrier and panel.sh edits.  agy deliberately not fired.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
